-- #2840 WITNESS 1 of 2: the alias spelling over a DEPTH-3 re-export chain.
--
-- Independent of `s8-xmod-reexport-alias-constrained/` in the one dimension
-- that could have made that row a depth-1 accident: `R` names `lib.hop3`,
-- which is three hops from the definer `lib.decl`, so the alias local `R.f`
-- can only reach the dict-name set through a resolution that CHASES the
-- chain (`graphPubDefiners`), not through one that looks one module back.
--
-- GROUND TRUTH, HAND-DERIVED FROM THE DECLARATIONS: `f : Num a => a -> a`,
-- `f x = x + 1`; `R.f 1` instantiates at `Int` (the literal defaults the
-- `Num` goal), so the program prints `2` on every verb.
import lib.hop3 as R

main = println (R.f 1)
